{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return deadline","requirement":"A landlord may not take a security deposit above one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account paying 5% per year, and must return it with an itemized list of damages within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent deposit; 5% per year interest; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Any lease or tenancy of residential real property in Massachusetts; applies to any lessor or agent who accepts a security deposit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"all residential rentals"},"exemptions":"Liability of a successor in interest does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter sixty, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"If the landlord fails to hold the deposit in a separate account, transfer it to a successor, or return it within 30 days, the tenant is awarded three times the deposit or balance plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees; the landlord also forfeits any right to retain the deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on upfront charges at the start of a tenancy","requirement":"A landlord or agent may require only first and last full months' rent, a one-month security deposit, and key-and-lock cost; a fee in lieu of a deposit is optional and capped at one month's rent in total.","key_value":"first month's rent + last month's rent + 1 month deposit + key and lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Amounts required of a tenant or prospective tenant at or before the start of any residential tenancy in Massachusetts, and any later demand for advance rent or a larger deposit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"all residential rentals"},"exemptions":"A fee in lieu of a security deposit is allowed only if the executive office of housing and livable communities authorizes it by regulation; the tenant may choose a full deposit or opt out.","penalty":"Not stated for charging amounts above the cap; a landlord who enforces a conflicting lease provision or seeks a waiver of the section forfeits the right to retain any part of the security deposit.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:\n(i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and,\n(ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
